@whycantweeatabortedbabies6259
Buys car complains about something that’s clearly obvious from the get go.
Or doesn’t even have the car and just here to complain about something they don’t even have.

@FreshMahogany our full coverage replacement value insurance in Southern Ontario 1,560 (Canadian dollars)
We have a claim free clean driving history.
It is always worth shopping around.

@zzackkkk the Tesla app is showing 50% charge and range estimate of 150 miles.
My wife has been out and about!
Tomorrow morning, it will be at 80% again, for $1.64 Canadian.

@curseknight5 nope... still no rattles or noises for us at the 110,000km (68,000 mile) mark.  We would obviously hear them more so as the vehicle has no engine noise to cover them up.  Also, we are but one data point.  
However, looking at the reported issues from others (who haters will say have drank the Kool-Aid), I think that we are typical.
I find the cabin to be quiet even with winter tires on, as  the engineers have probabably made it a priority to make the cabin soundproofing a priority.

@zzackkkk 
This morning after overnight charging to 80%, we are showing a real-world expected range of 220 miles, more than enough for our daily driving.  We start every day with that level.
If we needed more, I could have tapped the app to get 100% charge overnight for a 275 mile range.  (Lower than normal due to subzero weather here in Ontario)

@wemakecookie side point
Roundabouts: another thing North Americans have an issue with!
We're starting to get them here in Southern Ontario.  I have done road trips in Europe and loved how they kept traffic flowing at interchanges and intersections.

​@kev60625 
@reidconti said this above:
"I had the same question, just checked it out today. If you look VERY closely at the bumper-mounted reflectors (that look identical to the ones on first-gen 3s), there's a thin translucent white strip. This acts as a repeater for the signals and presumably brake lights when the trunk lid is lifted. Was a huge surprise to me because at first glance I thought they were the same p/n as the reflectors on my 2018."

@reidconti I was talking about the missing stalks.
I don’t know, what you try to explain.
By the way: I drive a Model Y Long Range (22).

