@G82Watts BMW!?!?!
I was for 25 years a BMW fan, and loved their classy but unpretentious style!  I have owned a total of 6 of them during this period (last one was a 2011 330i convertible... which is now my wife's car).  But BMW changed style, very clearly for the worse... they have become ugly, heavy (that they are, but I mean heavy-looking), pretentious... especially with the cancerous growth of their kidneys!  
If it is your definition of a car giving esthetic emotions... then I agree... negative ones!

@username65585no the entire world use kilometers as standard, including United States. All imperial units are defined by NIST through a constant multiplier on metric.

In the meantime, the British and United States, through its long tradition of positivism, tend to leave tradition in place and not forcing a transition. That's the freedom we own. We don't need to choose between science and tradition, instead we have both.

Namely, we Americans use both kilometers and miles, put men on the moon, and created Tesla.

